# one-home.manifest — the files that are allowed to exist twice, and the rule
# that they must then say the same thing.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL. Without it `check-one-home.sh` prints "no
# one-home.manifest at the repo root, so NOTHING is checked here" on every
# commit, for ever. A gate that announces on every commit that it is checking
# nothing does not read as a gap after the third day; it reads as scenery, and
# nobody sees it again. That is measured rather than supposed: it had been
# printing in at least one project for as long as the hook had been installed
# before anybody mentioned it (2026-09-25).
#
# ── THE DIRECTIVES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   pair       <canonical> <copy>        both in THIS repo; must hash match
#   dir        <canonical> <copy>        every file present in BOTH must match
#   fleet-pair <fleet-path> <local>      canonical lives in the hephaestus
#                                        checkout, which is a different repo
#   fleet-dir  <fleet-dir>  <local-dir>  same, for a whole directory
#   dup-ok     <path>                    this content may have a second home
#
# The canonical side is written FIRST and is the one to edit. A mismatch names
# it, so you never have to work out which copy is the real one.
#
# A fleet path is relative to the hephaestus checkout. It is found via
# HEPHAESTUS_ROOT, then a sibling directory, then ~/the-factory/hephaestus. When
# none of those exist the fleet directives become notes rather than refusals,
# because a clone on a machine without hephaestus still has to be committable.
#
# ── WHAT IS DECLARED BELOW ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The hooks, because those are the copies that actually drift. install-project.sh
# copies them in, and from that moment the project has a second home for every
# one of them with nothing comparing the two. Three live, running hooks were once
# found wrong in both copies, differently, which is the failure this prevents.

fleet-dir tools/claude-setup/templates/scripts/hooks scripts/hooks
fleet-dir tools/claude-setup/hooks .githooks

# empty-remote-gate.sh exists in the fleet ONLY under tools/claude-setup/hooks,
# and it also has a copy in scripts/hooks here. That second copy is not covered
# by either fleet-dir above, so nothing was updating it: sixteen repositories
# were carrying a stale gate that looked current because an identical one sat
# beside it in .githooks. Named explicitly so the fleet owns both.
fleet-pair tools/claude-setup/hooks/empty-remote-gate.sh scripts/hooks/empty-remote-gate.sh

# ── ADD YOUR OWN BELOW ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Anything this project keeps in two places goes here. A systemd unit that is
# both in the repo and installed, a config the build copies, a schema shared
# between a backend and a frontend. If a copy is deliberate and the two are
# allowed to differ, say so with dup-ok and write the reason beside it, because
# an exception nobody can justify later gets widened by whoever trips over it.
